WEBVTT

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:03.600
A contractor says the software is
delivered.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.900
Finance sees a funded escrow.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:11.933
Legal still needs the exact artifact,
client acceptance, and a clear view of

00:00:11.933 --> 00:00:13.333
anything blocking release.

00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:14.733
This is Accord.

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:19.167
Start with the accepted delivery fixture.

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:25.200
Accord compares the agreed terms with the
observed delivery and escrow state.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.200
All checks pass, producing ready for human
review.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.233
The six demonstration scenarios are
synthetic.

00:00:32.233 --> 00:00:34.233
No payment is authorized.

00:00:35.633 --> 00:00:40.100
Change the delivered artifact and the
commitment no longer matches.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:45.933
Accord highlights the failing row, places
the review on hold, and records the

00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:46.367
reason.

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:49.500
A funded escrow cannot repair broken
evidence.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:56.633
An open dispute also blocks review, even
when the document matches.

00:00:56.633 --> 00:01:01.867
The policy checks the beneficiary, amount,
client acceptance, challenge period,

00:01:01.867 --> 00:01:03.933
finality, and snapshot freshness.

00:01:03.933 --> 00:01:07.600
Each condition has an explicit failure
reason.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.267
The actual TypeScript workflow uses the
official Chainlink CRE SDK.

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:17.433
HTTP consensus establishes the delivery
content.

00:01:17.433 --> 00:01:23.233
A finalized EVM header pins the escrow
read to one block.

00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:26.367
Client acceptance comes from the contract.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:30.067
The same deterministic policy produces the
receipt.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:37.800
This is the saved output from a successful
official CRE CLI simulation.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:42.567
Matching delivery returned review ready,
with human authorization required.

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:48.367
This run used a private EVM and controlled
local HTTP providers.

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:49.967
Broadcasting was disabled.

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:56.333
A second actual CLI run changed the
delivery bytes.

00:01:56.333 --> 00:02:01.867
The workflow executed successfully and
returned hold, with delivery commitment

00:02:01.867 --> 00:02:02.400
mismatch.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.600
Both simulations exited zero.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:09.567
These logs demonstrate local
orchestration, not a live decentralized

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:11.233
oracle network deployment.

00:02:12.633 --> 00:02:17.633
Import the portable result into the desk
to reproduce its recorded fingerprint.

00:02:17.633 --> 00:02:22.633
Accord validates the file and evaluates
the evidence at its original time.

00:02:22.633 --> 00:02:25.133
The import is unsigned historical replay.

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:29.733
It does not authenticate the source or
query a live chain.

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:35.800
Accord turns scattered delivery evidence
into a reproducible review record.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:39.500
The public source and demo are available
now.

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:43.233
The human retains legal judgment and
payment authorization.
